From d5545778a8e71474d5ac3fd6d0d8158a557e6656 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LGA1150 <9155358+LGA1150@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 16:14:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: eip93 - add GCM with payload-only bulk CTR

Generic GCM prepends a 16-byte tag-mask block to the CTR scatterlists.
EIP93's DMA write-alignment checks then bounce otherwise aligned in-place
payloads. A partial final block can also force full-record bounce buffers.

Register gcm-aes-eip93 using the existing hardware CTR driver and a
synchronous GHASH transform. Compute AES_K(J0) separately in software,
submit only whole DMA-cache-line payload extents to CTR from counter 2,
and handle the remaining bytes in software. Slice SG metadata without
modifying caller lists or mapping AAD, authentication tags or the CPU tail.
Use request-local SG storage for the common one/two-entry case.

Authenticate RX ciphertext before decryption so a bad tag cannot overwrite
in-place input. Compute the TX tag after CTR completion. Preserve accepted
backlog, early callbacks, synchronous completion and terminal error rules.
Restrict hardware key-size adjustment to skcipher templates now that a
non-authenc AES AEAD is present in the registration table.

Aligned private in-place buffers can use the existing direct DMA path.
Misaligned/fragmented requests retain the child's bounce and CTR controls.
This does not change kTLS allocations or overwrite cloned TCP buffers.

Validation: host GCC W=1; 5,176 QEMU differential cases across synchronous,
BH asynchronous, backlog and callback-before-return CTR fixtures; 16
requests in flight and submission/completion errors; both TLS versions and
all recv/send/splice directions with an asynchronous software CTR child.
Hardware DMA correctness and performance need device testing.

OpenAI Codex assisted with implementation, validation and this changelog.
---
